    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency trio of **Jonathan Aranda** (66.42), **Lawrence Butler** (65.46), and **Luis Arraez** (63.51). **Jonathan Aranda** benefits from a favorable matchup against Alcantara and a prime #2 hole promotion, while **Lawrence Butler** leverages a strong platoon edge against the right-handed Burrows to secure our highest outfield upside. Despite the wind-in risk at the park, **Luis Arraez** remains a staple in our lineup given the matchup against Taillon, where his plate discipline profiles well against a middle-of-the-road xERA. **Jung Hoo Lee** also presents a strong start at 61.18, assuming he hits in the middle of the order, as his contact-oriented profile pairs perfectly with the volume we need to keep pace in AVG.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved our bench, where **Gleyber Torres** (49.11) narrowly missed the final cut. While **Gleyber Torres** carries respectable raw power, his score was suppressed by a poor platoon dynamic against Castillo; we ultimately prioritized the higher-upside platoon splits of **Matt Chapman** and **Bryson Stott**. We are monitoring the status of **Geraldo Perdomo** (49.67) and **Taylor Ward** (48.54), both of whom fall into the marginal category. **Taylor Ward** is dealing with an elite test against Gausman, but his lead-off spot keeps him viable. We are exercising caution with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.23); facing deGrom is a volatility trap, though we cannot reasonably bench a player of his caliber. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** both sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, meaning we are relying on **Drew Gilbert** and **Matt Chapman** to provide sufficient floor points to navigate today\u2019s tougher SP assignments.",
